invariant: INV-22
file: src/tcp_read.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_read_in_place answers the peer's close_notify with this side's
  own, as TLS 1.2 required and RFC 9846 section 6.1 dropped. The send comes
  from inside a read that calls no callback (INV-28), which colibri's
  adapter does not expect, so the alert is lost;
  bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test counts the send.

--- old
        tlsi_close_read_side(t);
        result->consumed = w->opened;
        return CH_ECLOSED;
--- new
        tlsi_close_read_side(t);
        (void)tlsi_send_alert(t, 1, ALERT_CLOSE_NOTIFY);
        result->consumed = w->opened;
        return CH_ECLOSED;
